# Project Inputs
**Acme Workshop | automated assembly cell investment**

The proposed line replaces outsourced assembly and creates additional capacity. The request includes installation and commissioning, with production beginning in January 2027. Amounts are in dollars.

Approval requires a positive discounted return, sufficient operating capacity and a credible maintenance plan.

| Input || Value |
| --- || --- |
| Equipment || 650000 {:,.2f} {::>} |
| Installation || 85000 {:,.2f} {::>} |
| Training || 25000 {:,.2f} {::>} |
| Initial capital || = B2 + B3 + B4 {:,.2f} {::>} |
| Annual capacity || 18000 |
| Year-one utilization || 0.55 {:.1%} |
| Annual utilization increase || 0.04 {:.1%} |
| Price per unit || 95 {:,.2f} {::>} |
| Variable cost per unit || 48 {:,.2f} {::>} |
| Fixed operating cost || 165000 {:,.2f} {::>} |
| Maintenance || 22000 {:,.2f} {::>} |
| Annual escalation || 0.025 {:.1%} |
| Useful life || 10 |
| Residual value || 60000 {:,.2f} {::>} |
| Working capital ratio || 0.12 {:.1%} |
| Tax rate || 0.25 {:.1%} |
| Discount rate || 0.12 {:.1%} |
| Finance rate || 0.08 {:.1%} |
| Reinvestment rate || 0.06 {:.1%} |

# Operating Plan
**Capacity ramp and ten-year operating case**

Utilization rises from 55% to 91% over the equipment life. Selling prices and operating costs escalate at 2.5% annually. Tax is charged on operating profit; the projected case has positive taxable earnings throughout.

Working capital is funded at commissioning and recovered when the cell is retired. Residual proceeds equal the remaining book value.

