# Decision
**Investment committee | economics and execution**

The base case clears the return hurdle, but authorization remains conditional on installation quotes, staffing and the production ramp. Dated and periodic returns are shown together because commissioning and year-end cash receipts follow actual calendar dates.

| Metric || Value |
| --- || --- |
| Initial funding || = -@["Cash Flows"::G2] {:,.2f} {::>} |
| Discount rate || = @["Project Inputs"::["Discount rate","Value"]] {:.1%} |
| Periodic NPV || = @["Cash Flows"::G2] + npv(B3, @["Cash Flows"::G3:G12]) {:,.2f} {::>} |
| Periodic IRR || = irr(@["Cash Flows"::G2:G12]) {:.1%} |
| Modified IRR || = mirr(@["Cash Flows"::G2:G12], @["Project Inputs"::["Finance rate","Value"]], @["Project Inputs"::["Reinvestment rate","Value"]]) {:.1%} |
| Dated NPV || = xnpv(B3, @["Cash Flows"::G2:G12], @["Cash Flows"::B2:B12]) {:,.2f} {::>} |
| Dated IRR || = xirr(@["Cash Flows"::G2:G12], @["Cash Flows"::B2:B12]) {:.1%} |
| Decision at discount rate || = if(B7 > 0, "Positive NPV", "Below hurdle") |
| Lifetime cash receipts || = sum(@["Cash Flows"::G3:G12]) {:,.2f} {::>} |
| Net cash surplus || = sum(@["Cash Flows"::G2:G12]) {:,.2f} {::>} |
| Peak annual revenue || = max(@["Operating Plan"::B6:K6]) {:,.2f} {::>} |
| Year-one contribution || = @["Operating Plan"::["Contribution","2027"]] {:,.2f} {::>} |
| Final utilization || = @["Operating Plan"::["Utilization","2036"]] {:.1%} |
| Approval status || Pending investment committee |
| Execution risk || Ramp-up training and planned shutdown |

# Sensitivity
**NPV | discount rate and commissioning overrun**

The downside grid holds operating performance unchanged and increases equipment, installation and training expenditure. It is intended to support the contingency allowance discussion, not replace a separate utilization downside case.

